  "slug": "nasutoceratops",
  "summary": "Nasutoceratops was a horned dinosaur that lived in what is now Utah about 76 million years ago. Its fossils were found in the Kaiparowits Formation from 2006 onward, and it was named in 2013 for its large nose and in honor of paleontologist Alan Titus.\n\nThe known fossils include a nearly complete skull, parts of the skeleton, and rare skin impressions. Nasutoceratops had a short, deep snout, a low nasal horn, and exceptionally long brow horns that curved forward and outward. It was an early-diverging member of the centrosaurine group of horned dinosaurs and the first known from the formation. Its fossils add evidence about the diversity of dinosaurs living on Laramidia, an island continent during the Late Cretaceous. The functions of its horns and frill remain uncertain.",
